A||N||3||johnt671||Headliner||||5||
Z||000000||johnt671||11-06-2001||09:44 AM||||I know this has been covered to death, but I'm confused one point.  In the other threads on replacement, it said to remove all the old material from the headliner backing.  My headliner is gone and all I have is the board with a coating of old glue that flakes off with what looks like fiberglass matting.  Does this matting have to be removed also before installing a new headliner or does it stay on?||||reg||5
Z||000001||Oreif||11-06-2001||09:57 AM||||No, Just use a stiff nylon brush and remove the loose stuff. It will make it smooth so that the glue will hold the new headliner.<P>Here is what mine looked like after brushing.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/headl_3.jpg"> <P>------------------<BR>            <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">          <BR><FONT SIZE="1"><B><I>Happiness isn't around the corner...<BR>Happiness IS the corner.</I></B></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Monkeyman||11-06-2001||12:16 PM||||Orf is right.  Let me add that a coating of fiberglass resin (not mat) over both sides will not only help the glue to stick, but will also strengthen the board.  Coat it fairly thick.  Once it dries, you'll be able to pick up the board from one side without fear of it breaking.  (Mine was in a few pieces.  Once I covered it, my dog [big German Shepherd] could stand on it without leaving a mark.)||||reg||1
Z||000003||bHooper||11-06-2001||08:11 PM||||you can also use poly urethane... but let it air out for a week or so (outside) b4 reinstallation.<P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR><FONT SIZE="3"><FONT COLOR="red"><B>Red</B></FONT></FONT> 86 GT 5 speed<BR><FONT SIZE="3"><B>Black</B></FONT> <u>86 SE Automatic</u>||||reg||1
